          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "4c108074-72b9-4db3-a248-c736b9ad2638",
          "type": "column",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "1f91cc44-df96-49d5-ac74-4bc200a0759d",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "The development of AAA games typically involves large teams- often multiple large teams- of developers working on different aspects of the game, from design, art, &amp; programming to testing, marketing, &amp; publishing. This can result in lengthy development cycles &amp; significant costs. Despite the high costs, these kinds of games can be extremely profitable, with some titles selling millions of copies &amp; generating hundreds of millions of dollars in revenue, contributing greatly to videogames’ status as the most profitable entertainment industry on Earth. In recent years though, AAA developers seem to be releasing fewer blockbuster titles &amp; an increasing market share is being taken up by indies &amp; <a href=\"#/mobile-gaming\">mobile games</a>."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
